{"archetypes":[{"name":"doc-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"design-log-publish.md has multiple prose locations describing render-cache staging behavior; checks that every stale claim is replaced and the new section's bullet list is internally consistent with the planned code changes.","prompt_body":"Read scripts/design-log-publish.md and locate every prose location that describes render-cache staging behavior, including the script-purpose paragraph at item 5 (currently the sentence about 'Symlinks at the top level are skipped; render-cache/ itself must be a real directory') and any later sections. Verify that after the planned additions and replacements there are no remaining stale claims that understate the new fail-closed posture, and check whether the Tests section needs updating to reference the new render-cache symlink harness cases. Confirm the planned 'render-cache symlink rejection' section's bullet list matches exactly the two new guards in the code (tree-wide find check and per-file [[ -L ]] recheck) with no extra or missing bullets. Check whether any other sentence in the document implicitly contradicts the new deeper-symlink rejection. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"insertion-anchor","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan cites 'current line 367' as the rc_root insertion point, but line 367 in the actual file is the closing brace of the rc_root error-handler block, not the rc_root assignment itself; ambiguous anchor descriptions can cause an implementer to insert inside a compound statement.","prompt_body":"Read scripts/design-log-publish.sh and cross-check every code-insertion anchor cited in the plan against the actual current file content. Specifically, verify whether the plan's description 'insert immediately after rc_root=$(cd ...) (current line 367)' accurately identifies the insertion location: determine whether line 367 is the rc_root assignment line or the closing brace of its || { ... } error-handler block, and confirm that inserting the tree-wide symlink check between line 367 and line 368 places it after the full error-handler and before the mktemp allocation. Apply the same check to the per-file recheck anchor described as 'after rel=${f#...} (current line 387) and before design_publish_stage_file (current line 388)' — verify no off-by-one would place the check inside an unintended block or after the staging call. Flag any anchor where the English prose and the cited line number refer to logically different positions in the script. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
